            </div>
            <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
              Every legitimate GST notice must bear a system-generated <strong>Document Identification Number (DIN)</strong> under CBIC Circular No. 122/41/2019-GST. Verify the DIN on <code class="font-mono text-[11px] bg-subtle px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">cbic.gov.in</code>. If the DIN is missing, the notice is legally invalid (non-est). Always record this as your primary preliminary objection.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-base bg-surface p-6 shadow-sm">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
              <span class="flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-accent/10 font-mono text-sm font-bold text-accent">02</span>
              <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-base">Perform Invoice-Level Reconciliation</h3>
            </div>
            <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
              Cross-examine the discrepancy cited in the notice against your books of accounts. For ITC differences, reconcile monthly <a href="/gstr-2b-reconciliation-tool" class="text-accent hover:underline font-medium">GSTR-2B vs GSTR-3B</a>. For turnover differences, compare GSTR-1 outward tax with GSTR-3B tax paid and audited financial ledgers.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-base bg-surface p-6 shadow-sm">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
              <span class="flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-accent/10 font-mono text-sm font-bold text-accent">03</span>
              <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-base">Draft Submissions & Hearing Prayer</h3>
            </div>
